Z||000000||fieroboy||04-02-2000||11:52 AM||||i have a 86se and it need painting real bad.<BR>It has been painted before but not very good.<BR>How do I strip all the old paint off the car?<BR>Is sanding or a chemical stripper the best way ? Is it easy to do? I dont have much budget for the paint job so if i do the stripping or sanding, i might be able to save a on the paint job when i take it to the paint shop. This is a great forum so i know someone can help me.<P>fieroboy||||reg||5
Z||000001||DiggityDan||04-02-2000||12:34 PM||||You don't necessarily have to take all of the paint off. just enough to get a smooth finish. Elbow grease would be the only way to go. I'm sure chemicals could eat through the plastic on your car. This part is definately why painting is expensive. If you do all of this yourself, you could probably find someone to shoot paint for a reasonable price.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-02-2000||01:17 PM||||There is a chemical stripper available that is safe for the plastic. Bumper Stripper- about $10 for a spray can.||||reg||1
